.TH REBUILD 8 "November 2026" "TeraStation TS5800D" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rebuild \- replace failed drives and recover RAID arrays on TeraStation TS5800D
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rebuild
[\fI1\-8\fR | \fI/dev/sdX\fR | \fB\-\-init\-storage\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rebuild
is an assisted disk replacement and disaster recovery tool for the Buffalo TeraStation
TS5800D. It automatically elevates to root via
.BR sudo (8),
clones the GPT partition layout from a healthy active member, re-integrates OS mirrors
.RI ( /dev/md0 ", " /dev/md1 ),
installs GRUB on the replacement disk, and queues RAID-5 data recovery
.RI ( /dev/md2 ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B (no arguments)
If a single failed or missing disk is detected, prompts to rebuild it automatically;
otherwise displays usage summary.
.TP
.I 1\-8
Rebuild the specified physical chassis bay number (e.g.,
.BR "rebuild 2" ).
.TP
.I /dev/sdX
Rebuild the specified kernel block device (e.g.,
.BR "rebuild /dev/sdb" ).
.TP
.B \-\-init\-storage
Disaster recovery mode. Wipes and recreates GPT partitions, OS mirrors
.RI ( md0 ", " md1 ),
RAID-5 storage array
.RI ( md2 ),
.IR /etc/mdadm/mdadm.conf ,
and GRUB across all 8 disks. Requires typing
.B INITIALIZE
to confirm.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show brief usage summary and exit.
.SH SAFEGUARDS
Refuses to overwrite healthy online members or drives currently rebuilding.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR status (8),
.BR mdadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Marcelo Santos \- ActionSys
